IMPORT prelude

-- Competition and Consumer Act 2010 (Cth) -- the dates for the claims encoding, in one small module.
--
-- It uses only the built-in date functions (DATE_FROM_DMY, DATE_SERIAL, DATE_FROM_SERIAL, DATE_DAY, DATE_MONTH,
-- DATE_YEAR), not the daydate library. The stable l4 has no comparison on dates, so dates are compared by serial.
--
-- "Within 3 years after" a day, "6 years after the day", "12 years following" an act, "10 years of the supply": each is
-- read with the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 (borrowed, not deposited): the day of the event is excluded (s 36(1)) and a
-- year is 12 months (s 2G: a month ends immediately before the corresponding day of the next month, or at the end of
-- that month if it has no corresponding day). So the period starts the day after the event and its last day is the day
-- before the corresponding day n years on: an event on 10 March 2023 gives 10 March 2026 as the last day of 3 years.
-- A last day on a Saturday, Sunday or public holiday is NOT moved (Acts Interpretation Act s 36(2)); see NOTES.md, fork F6.
--
-- Sourced from the Federal Register of Legislation, Commonwealth of Australia, CC BY 4.0 (SOURCE-LICENSE.md).
-- BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Dates for the Competition and Consumer Act 2010 claims encoding`

GIVEN d IS A NUMBER, m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DATE
`the calendar date` d m y MEANS DATE_FROM_DMY d m y

-- Plain days from one day to another (negative if the second is earlier).
GIVEN `the start` IS A DATE, `the end` IS A DATE
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the days from` `the start` `to` `the end` MEANS DATE_SERIAL `the end` MINUS DATE_SERIAL `the start`

-- The day a given number of plain days after a day.
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the start` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the date` n `days after` `the start` MEANS DATE_FROM_SERIAL (DATE_SERIAL `the start` PLUS n)

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is after` b IF DATE_SERIAL a GREATER THAN DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the day` a `is on or before` b IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the later of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT LEAST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

GIVEN a IS A DATE, b IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the earlier of` a `and` b MEANS
    IF DATE_SERIAL a AT MOST DATE_SERIAL b
    THEN a
    ELSE b

-- The number of days in a calendar month (the first of the next month, less the first of this month).
GIVEN m IS A NUMBER, y IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`the length of month` m `of` y MEANS
    IF m EQUALS 12
    THEN 31
    ELSE DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 (m PLUS 1) y) MINUS DATE_SERIAL (DATE_FROM_DMY 1 m y)

-- The last day of a period of n whole years after a day, under the Acts Interpretation Act 1901 ss 2G, 36(1):
-- the period starts the next day and ends immediately before the corresponding day n years on, or at the end of the
-- month where that month has no corresponding day (a period starting on 29 February).
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER, `the day of the event` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`the last day of` n `years after` `the day of the event` MEANS
    IF `the day number` AT MOST `the length of month` `the month number` `of` `the target year`
    THEN `the date` (0 MINUS 1) `days after` (DATE_FROM_DMY `the day number` `the month number` `the target year`)
    ELSE DATE_FROM_DMY (`the length of month` `the month number` `of` `the target year`) `the month number` `the target year`
    WHERE
        `the first day` MEANS `the date` 1 `days after` `the day of the event`
        `the day number` MEANS DATE_DAY `the first day`
        `the month number` MEANS DATE_MONTH `the first day`
        `the target year` MEANS DATE_YEAR `the first day` PLUS n
